## Original Content
Billionaire investor Ray Dalio said the the debt buyback announcement this week fits into a larger pattern that could signal a forthcoming debt crisis.

## Summary
Billionaire investor Ray Dalio warned that this week's debt buyback announcement by Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent fits into a larger pattern signaling that a US debt crisis may be drawing closer. In response to these concerns, Dalio recommended holding gold and bitcoin as protective assets.

## Key Points
- Ray Dalio views the recent Treasury debt buyback announcement as part of a broader pattern pointing toward a potential debt crisis
- Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent's debt buyback move was the specific trigger for Dalio's warning
- Dalio recommends gold as a hedge against the anticipated debt crisis
- Dalio also recommends bitcoin as a hedge against fiscal instability


